HST Office: Draw's ribbon as in the approved 1.0.2 mockup (16/11/2026).

- Home: Clipboard, Shapes, Shape Styles and Editing are groups of three rows (large buttons over the three rows,
  small buttons filling their columns top to bottom, caption in row 3, separator over four rows). Clipboard:
  Paste, then Cut, Copy, Format Painter labelled (Paste Special stays in the Paste menu). Font and Paragraph
  are two icon-only rows. Paragraph: bullets, numbering, indents and a Line Spacing menu (spacing 1, 1.5, 2,
  increase or decrease paragraph spacing); the four alignments; a column of Text Direction and Align Text
  menus on the same two rows. Left-to-right, right-to-left and the hanging indent leave the tab (Paragraph
  dialog). The Drawing group becomes Shapes (Shapes menu and Text Box large, Line, Connectors and Callout
  as an icon column), Shape Styles (the Styles deck as a large button, Fill, Outline and Shadow labelled,
  the Area dialog behind the corner button) and Arrange (an Arrange menu with the order commands, Group,
  Ungroup and Rotate, and the Align menu, both large).
- Edit PDF leaves Home and opens the PDF tab (Text Box, Image, Redact large).
- Insert: Images, Illustrations and Media make one Illustrations group; Fontwork joins Text, and its four
  shaping tools move to the shape context tab; Fields and Symbols follow the mockup's order.
- Arrange, Page, PDF, Review, View, Help and Extension: large buttons beside columns of small labelled buttons
  as in the mockup (Distribute joins Arrange, Flip Vertical and Flip Horizontal show directly in Rotate and
  Flip); Page Setup, PDF and Proofing keep one large button, Order is a column of three small ones.
- Commands with a drop-down controller (Underline, Bullets, Numbering, Table, Fill, Outline, Align,
  Distribute, Connectors) are drop-down buttons. Every command is an existing one.
New groups: gdHomeHstShapes, gdHomeHstArrange, gdExportHstPdfEdit (was gdHomeHstPdfEdit), gdDrawHstFontwork;
removed: gdInsertGraphic, gdInsertFontwork, gdInsertMedia. The new strings get empty entries in the
Vietnamese sd/messages.po, filled by l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl; the new menu items take their command labels
(sdraw.suppr).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
